# Impossible Inferno: "deals 6 damage to target creature. Delirium - If there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard,
# exile the top card of your library. You may play it until the end of your next turn" (CR 120.3, 207.2c, 701.13a, 611.2a). On turn 1 Black
# Lotus pays for a Wheel of Fortune that puts a sorcery (the Wheel), an artifact (the Lotus), an artifact creature (Ornithopter) and a land
# (the Islands) into Bot1's graveyard: four types. Bot2 draws a Black Lotus and a Glacial Wall (0/7). On turn 3 the Inferno cannot target a
# player; aimed at the Wall it leaves it alive with exactly 6 damage, and exiles Bot1's top card, a Mountain (Bot2's library is untouched).
# The Mountain is not played that turn, and is played on turn 5 as the land for the turn, the end of Bot1's next turn.

